---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Sentiment"
  description="An unscientific one-response-per-browser poll about a possible combination. Not a share vote and not a representative sample."
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Unscientific · one response per browser</p>
    <h1>Which way do holders lean today?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      If TSLA shareholders are asked to vote on a combination with SpaceX, which way do you lean
      today? There is no proposal. This question is not that vote.
    </p>
    <ul class="clean">
      <li>Not a scientific poll. People who find this site are not a sample of shareholders.</li>
      <li>Not weighted by shares. One browser, one stored response.</li>
      <li>The id lives in an HttpOnly cookie. Clearing site data allows another response. That is a limit of the design, not a security claim.</li>
      <li>Counts come only from the database. This page never shows a made-up tally.</li>
    </ul>
    <form id="poll-form" class="poll">
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="visually-hidden">Your lean, if a combination is proposed later</legend>
        <label class="choice">
          <input type="radio" name="choice" value="favor" required />
          <span><strong>Lean in favor</strong><br />You would lean toward voting yes, on terms you have not seen.</span>
        </label>
        <label class="choice">
          <input type="radio" name="choice" value="against" />
          <span><strong>Lean against</strong><br />You would lean toward voting no, on terms you have not seen.</span>
        </label>
        <label class="choice">
          <input type="radio" name="choice" value="undecided" />
          <span><strong>Undecided</strong><br />You are waiting for a proxy, or you do not have a lean.</span>
        </label>
      </fieldset>
      <button type="submit">Store my response</button>
      <p id="poll-status" class="status" role="status">Loading the tally…</p>
      <div id="poll-results" class="tally" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </form>
  </div>
</Base>

<script>
  import { mountPoll } from "../scripts/poll";
  mountPoll();
</script>
